    "steps": [
      "Heat the canola oil in a large soup pot over medium heat. Cook the garlic and onion for about 3 minutes, until the onion is translucent.",
      "Add the zucchini, jalapeño and yellow squash. Stir now and then for about 3 minutes, until softened.",
      "Stir in the spinach and the cilantro for the soup. Cook for about 3 minutes, until wilted.",
      "Pour in the broth and bring to a boil. Lower the heat and simmer for 40 minutes, stirring occasionally.",
      "Season with the cumin, salt and pepper, then cook for 5 minutes more.",
      "Let the soup cool a little, until it is no longer steaming hard.",
      "Blend the soup in batches until smooth, filling the blender only partway and venting the lid.",
      "Strain the soup through a fine sieve back into the pot and discard the solids. Reheat gently until hot.",
      "Ladle into bowls and garnish, if you like, with the reserved cilantro sprigs, crumbled queso fresco and a drizzle of crema.",
      "You nailed it! Grab a plate and dig in."
